ns how overlapping colors in the input, when mapped to the same output location, are overwritten by the later input colors. I'm now testing these assumptions and refining the pattern based on Example 2.\n\n\n**Refining Color Overlays**\n\nI've zeroed in on the exact mechanism for color overwrites. It's a row-by-row, left-to-right drawing process. I'm now certain about the order of operations, and I can predict which colors will be visible in overlapping regions. I've reconfirmed that this pattern explains why some colors are seen and others are not in the test data. I'm now testing it across all examples.\n\n\n",
